Task 2: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) and Feature Insights 

Project Goal:
To conduct an in-depth statistical and visual exploration of the cleaned dataset to uncover patterns, validate assumptions, and generate actionable insights that guide the feature engineering and model selection process.

Key Outcomes & Skills:
a. Insight Generation: Derived statistical summaries and key feature distributions, providing a comprehensive understanding of the data's composition and inherent variability.

b. Relationship Mapping: Utilized correlation heatmaps (Seaborn) to quantify and visualize the relationships between all features, effectively identifying highly correlated features for potential reduction or transformation.

c. Data Storytelling: Created high-impact visualizations (Histograms, Scatter Plots) to showcase feature distributions and their correlation with the target variable, aiding in stakeholder communication.

d. Pre-Modeling Strategy: Based on EDA findings, defined a targeted strategy for feature engineering (e.g., creating interaction terms or polynomial features) to maximize model performance.

Technical Stack:
a. Category: Tool / Concept
b. Libraries: Pandas, Matplotlib, Seaborn
c. Concepts: Summary Statistics, Correlation Analysis, Distribution Visualization, Feature Engineering
